{
  "full_prompt_html": "<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Act as an experienced HR business partner, a learning and development specialist and a line manager who has onboarded many new hires.</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Build an onboarding plan for a new hire who is joining our team. [Paste the job description, the team structure and the start date.] [Paste any existing onboarding checklist or policies, if you have them.]</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Organize the plan in four parts:</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>1. Before Day One</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nList everything that must be ready on the first morning: equipment, system access, Microsoft 365 licenses, building access and a named buddy.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nAssign each item to an owner (manager, IT, HR or buddy) and a deadline relative to the start date.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>2. Days 1 to 30: Learn</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nSchedule the introductions the new hire needs, with the reason for each meeting.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nIdentify the three to five processes or systems they must understand first, and how they will learn each one.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nSet one small, real task they can finish in the first two weeks.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>3. Days 31 to 90: Contribute, Then Own</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nDefine what the new hire should own by day 60 and by day 90, based on the job description.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nWrite two or three measurable goals for the end of the 90 days.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nPlan check-ins at days 30, 60 and 90, with the questions the manager should ask at each one.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>4. Risks and Gaps</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nFlag any part of the role that the job description does not explain clearly.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nIdentify where the new hire will depend on one person for knowledge, and suggest a backup.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Deliver the plan as a week-by-week table for the first 30 days and a milestone table for days 31 to 90, followed by the pre-start checklist with owners and dates. Keep each entry to one line.</span></p>",
  "n": 3,
  "subject_area": "HR and people ops",
  "summary": "Plan a new hire’s first 90 days across pre-start readiness, introductions, early tasks, measurable goals, manager check-ins, and knowledge risks.",
  "title": "Build a 90-day onboarding plan for a new hire"
}
